        "# Hands-on 1 — Simple Linear Regression (SLR) with Python\n",
        "\n",
        "**Materia:** Machine Learning 2026B  \n",
        "**Alumno:** Yahir Valenzuela  \n",
        "**Docente:** José Antonio Aviña Méndez  \n",
        "\n",
        "## Fundamentos de la técnica SLR\n",
        "\n",
        "La Regresión Lineal Simple estudia la relación entre una variable independiente y una variable dependiente. El objetivo es encontrar una línea recta que represente la relación entre ambas variables.\n",
        "\n",
        "## Modelo matemático\n",
        "\n",
        "El artículo utiliza una función lineal con una pendiente `w` y un intercepto `b`. También utiliza funciones de pérdida como MSE y MAE para medir el error de las predicciones.\n",
        "\n",
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "id": "b71e119a",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "b71e119a"
      },
      "source": [
        "## Code 1 — Python Implementation of Simple Linear Regression\n",
        "\n",
        "Este bloque define la función de predicción, la función MSE, los datos de ejemplo y los parámetros del modelo."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": 1,
      "id": "c17c8aa2",
      "metadata": {
        "colab": {
          "base_uri": "https://localhost:8080/"
        },
        "id": "c17c8aa2",
        "outputId": "7b19a0ab-ee95-4c3b-c36a-82ced3036ecb"
      },
      "outputs": [
        {
          "output_type": "stream",
          "name": "stdout",
          "text": [
            "Predicted values: [1.8 2.6 3.4 4.2 5. ]\n",
            "MSE Loss: 0.920\n"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "source": [
        "import numpy as np\n",
        "\n",
        "def predict(x, w, b):\n",
        "    return w * x + b\n",
        "\n",
        "def mse_loss(y_pred, y_true):\n",
        "    return np.mean((y_pred - y_true) ** 2)\n",
        "\n",
        "# Example data\n",
        "x = np.array([1, 2, 3, 4, 5])       # Input data (independent variable)\n",
        "y_true = np.array([2, 4, 5, 4, 5])  # True output data (dependent variable)\n",
        "\n",
        "# Model parameters (slope and intercept)\n",
        "w = 0.8\n",
        "b = 1.0\n",
        "\n",
        "# Predict outputs\n",
        "y_pred = predict(x, w, b)\n",
        "\n",
        "# Calculate MSE loss\n",
        "loss = mse_loss(y_pred, y_true)\n",
        "\n",
        "print(f\"Predicted values: {y_pred}\")\n",
        "print(f\"MSE Loss: {loss:.3f}\")\n",
        "\n",
        "# Predicted values: [1.8 2.6 3.4 4.2 5.]\n",
        "# MSE Loss: 0.920"
      ]
    },
